would now be unfeasible in this strategically&nbsp;
important region." – The German Institute for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.040 --> 00:15:00.900
International and Security Affairs (SWP))
 
And if, with all this, Russia's Baltic Fleet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:06.060
is practically history, the future integration of&nbsp;
Ukraine into NATO would make the same happen with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.060 --> 00:15:10.140
the Black Sea Fleet, but that is another matter.
 
Sticking with the subject of Sweden, although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:14.700
this country has a relatively small army, it&nbsp;
brings to the alliance an important military&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:19.980
industry. And keep in mind that Swedish factories&nbsp;
produce not only small weapons, but advanced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:26.580
systems such as combat aircraft, missiles, tanks,&nbsp;
submarines, warships and air defense platforms.&nbsp;

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:31.080
("We believe that we will contribute to&nbsp;
the defense of the Allies. We don't have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:35.700
an Armed Forces as numerous as Finland, but&nbsp;
we have the most advanced technologies and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:40.560
very powerful Defense companies" – Teppo&nbsp;
Tauriainen, Swedish Ambassador to Spain)
 &nbsp;

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:44.940
In other words, Sweden's accession to&nbsp;
NATO is without exaggeration one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:49.200
biggest leaps in terms of security for&nbsp;
the whole of Europe in recent decades.
 &nbsp;

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:56.820
Putin's special military operation saw Russia&nbsp;
go from sharing just 841 km or 522 miles of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.820 --> 00:16:06.120
borders with NATO in 2021 to more than 2,100&nbsp;
km or 1,305 miles after Finland's entry. Now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:11.160
the integration of Sweden will mean that it will&nbsp;
also lose all its influence in the Baltic Sea. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:16.140
disaster in strategic terms is colossal.
 
